{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact M5 head 449979c2b64df66f6040a847602d61d9b836fa92 on builder/typed-core-m5-20261107, tree 2d82af13, all 29 paths, for request 053c4f4b under promise 3a9595b1 and review request da207eab. Ordinary effects, attention and item settlement now run from admitted typed instructions. I found one execution difference from main: a result clause that has observation rows and no effects now throws. No installed or installable definition can reach it, so it does not block this head. M6 must fix it (finding F1 below).\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main 3cb223b8 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Merge 4f7d442a has parents 80f2a75d and 3cb223b8, and against main it adds only the M4 note. The commit-message check passes: 6 checked, 0 flagged. The 29 paths are the derive source and tests, one platform test, the generated Page module, notes and six manifests. No dependency, lockfile, gate script, seal, grant, wire type, platform source or Wrangler file changes. packages/derive/src/judge.ts keeps blob 62248f2e, the same as main (SHA-256 86222a9f…).\n- The failed gate. I read gate.exit at a14c4150, tree 79e5555e: \"exit 1\". result.json records Node 135, Counting 56, and Plain 4,005 passed, 1 failed and 1 skipped. Native never ran. The one failure is \"a native service-generation effect holds its real local position, without fabricating a self fact\" in packages/platform/test/rules-scope-v13.test.ts, which threw \"effects have no admitted body context\". before.json and after.json are byte-equal: clean status, lockfile 5a717d43 and gate.sh 001c4b10. The summary records no unhandled error and no report error. The failed gate stays failed.\n- The isolated repair. The \"Follow-up after a gate\" section of docs/testing.md permits it, and the head meets each condition:\n  - Between a14c4150 and the head, only that test file, the M5 note and the six manifests change. No file imports the test file.\n  - The repair admits its one-effect probe through checkedPlatformData and passes that admitted body. Every case, assertion and expected value stays literal.\n  - The follow-up unit's original.test.ts and repaired.test.ts equal the file at a14c4150 and at the head, and repair.patch matches the commit.\n  - The platform test compiler exits 0. Its config includes test/. The four-case file exits 0 with 4 of 4 passing. The unreached Native phase exits 0 with 1,111 passed and 2 skipped. All 4,182 tracked hashes match before and after the follow-up.\n- The evidence. The six manifests hash to the SHA-256 values that the note cites. Their 300 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match. The effects unit's final-draft hashes equal the committed bytes of all 15 source and test paths it lists. Each of the two controls passes before and fails by assertion after.\n- The Page module. The asset freshness test ran in the gate's plain phase and passed, and assets.ts has not changed since a14c4150. GitHub reports run 42416131810 (Page browser scripts) as successful at a14c4150. Scope addendum 92117542 covers assets.ts.\n- The tests. Every existing assertion stays. The opening witness keeps its child.effects assertion and now also compares the complete effects, working map and opened item. The attribution witness now runs on cards with its `each` source written twice. The union removes duplicates, so the unchanged expectations also cover a shared source object. The `derived` helper now admits a probe definition instead of passing raw forms with a null body. New cases cover the nested-constant skip, a mutation after admission, a repeated true mark under free room, and the capture-order repair.\n- Semantics. An independent read of the packages/derive/src diff against main found these preserved:\n  - the order of refusal checks and their detail paths, and the bounds checks (most, slot full, member fit and list maximum);\n  - the order of effects, of attention, of list removals and additions, and of the attribution union;\n  - the absent-read skip, `clear`, and `sourceStated` for every admitted operand;\n  - `if` and then `unless` on the before-entry view, and the unbound-subject skip, where `conditionSubjects` keeps the old `also.` test and the walk into constants;\n  - each occurrence runs its own node and binder, even when two occurrences share one source object;\n  - a Native mark stays the declared object, and `join`, `ruleFor` and the `ran.clock` contribution do not change;\n  - `settlementMatches` is the old `itemSettledBy` body, and a repeated true mark stays new work;\n  - outcomes.ts changes only its import and its call. Main's synthetic form also went through `markOf` and `join(mark, 0)`.\n- M4 follow-ups. The M4 note now links the six manifests, and each SHA-256 matches. validate/sends.ts line 45 has not changed. M6 owns sends, so that fix stays with M6. judgeGuards and judgeGuard stay until M8.\n\nF1 (does not block; M6 must fix). When a result clause has no effects, runClause (handlers.ts lines 595 to 645) builds no body for it. If the clause has observation rows, runClause still calls `deriveEffects(j, [], [], null, null)`. At effects.ts line 119, deriveEffects now throws \"effects have no admitted body context\". Main ran the empty list with a null body and recorded the result. I reproduced this on extracted trees of both revisions. The case is the weigher platform data, with an act `go` whose `tell` has an `applied` clause with no effects and one `observes` row. The validator admits it. Delivering an `applied` result records `write` with no effects on main and throws TypeError on head.\n\nF1 does not block for three reasons:\n- Only platform data may state send-clause rows (validate/sends.ts line 68).\n- A definition from an input is validated without the platform option.\n- The Native catalog VERSIONS holds 63 definitions with 26 sends, and none states send-clause `observes`. So no installed or installable room reaches the throw at this head.\n\nNo gate case delivers a result to such a clause. forms-holds.test.ts covers only admission and reservation. Fix F1 in M6, which owns clause routes. Either accept a null body when both lists are empty, or capture a body for a clause that has only rows. Then add a witness that delivers that result and compares the recorded result with main's.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Execution now reads only what admission captured. Each instruction owns its plan, source and binder, and deriveEffects refuses a list that does not match its admitted body. That makes the adapter stricter than main. A caller that passes a sliced list, or an empty one, without its body now throws. Every production caller passes a matching body, except the path in F1. A definition that something mutates after admission now runs as admitted. The new ownership witness pins that behavior, and no production code mutates a declared definition.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The head changes no seal, grant, wire type, dependency or configuration, and judge.ts does not change. An input definition cannot reach F1. Capability arguments stay frozen copies. `joinReturnedEffects` is now public through `export * from \"./effects.ts\"`. It grants nothing: it only joins effects that a Native rule already returned.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Four notes:\n\n1. packages/derive/src/unsupported.ts lost its only importer, effects.ts, in this head. Delete it.\n2. guards.ts lines 96 to 100 keep the doc comment of the removed `unbound` helper, directly above the comment for readsUnbound.\n3. `alsoRead` in validate/sends.ts and `conditionSubjects` in program/condition-plan.ts walk the same names. One of them can serve both.\n4. `joinReturnedEffects` has one caller, outcomes.ts. Keep it out of the package's public exports.\n\nArchive request 64552d40 stays open. This approval does not turn the failed gate at a14c4150 into a pass.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fb2f0cdf954a8f737e669ce1053837be9bfd51d0","binding":"assigned","head":"449979c2b64df66f6040a847602d61d9b836fa92","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4230d69b3b5d7eba3c636288ca0ed71c127f48d0\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a06c3198dbe98010589f55fb222f085c6c0d5635\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0b0d278680c4dde3a9b278d4a76a547ef83223cc\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3a9595b12fe9e6d5800c519682297842399ed93d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c8c8569367016a10087a26e1b0801e5ea21e8c93","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}